# Brenz Presentation

Source: `@docs/architecture/brenz-architecture-presentation.md`. Design: `@docs/product/brenz-design-system-decision.md`.

## Rules
- Decide the root screen in `RootViewModel`: splash, welcome flow (no session), onboarding (profile without `onboardingCompleted`), Home with tab bar.
- Use one `NavigationStack` per tab and one route `enum` per feature. Open sheets with `.sheet`.
- Start reads with `.task` in the view.
- Publish errors as an optional `AuthError` or `AppError`. Use `isSubmitting` in forms.
- Keep ViewModels free of message logic: they only display the resolved `MessageKey`.
- Resolve keys with `String(localized: String.LocalizationValue(key))`. With arguments, use `String(format:)` and positional specifiers (`%1$@`).
- Add the dynamic message keys to the catalog with state "manual", in `en` and `es`.
- Pass `LocalizedStringResource` to fixed texts of `BrenzDesignSystem`. Pass `String` to dynamic texts (message, nickname, figures).
- Animate with native SwiftUI. Read motion and springs from the package tokens.
- Apply the package "Reduce Motion" modifier to every animation.
- Put `DayBoard` in `Presentation/Shared/`.
- Put the flow to delete a log in the History feature.

## Forbidden
- Do not import Firebase in Presentation.
- Do not write visible text in code or fixed colors.
- Do not choose messages inside a ViewModel.
- Do not use `Combine`.
- Do not add Lottie or another animation library.
- Do not translate the character nickname.
- Do not add loading screens in Home and History.
